# Keep the build context small and the image clean.
#
# Without this, `docker build` ships the whole working tree to the daemon — including
# .venv and node_modules, which are hundreds of megabytes and are rebuilt inside the image
# anyway — and `COPY backend/` would bake the developer's recourse.db into the image, so
# every container would start with one person's local decisions and audit trail instead of
# seeding itself.

# Dependencies — reinstalled in the image
.venv/
venv/
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]

# Local state that must never be baked in
.env
*.db
*.db-journal
**/.signal_cache.json

# Build output — the image builds its own
frontend/dist/
**/.smoke-shots/
**/.evidence-shots/

# Repo and tooling
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
*.log

# Docs are not needed at runtime
docs/
*.md
!README.md
